  "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=7\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-7$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-7$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $0$ | $-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/assets/debf9475589e7e242df986d1fffb8a97834d6ce550279fc82b0428001b661eaa.png)",
